From 93f8adcbffb7d01b74b9d3ce9aed90497fe86922 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mayur Panchal <mayur@canva.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 15:52:41 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] xradio: advertise management frame protection support

The XR819 driver does not advertise MFP_CAPABLE, which prevents
mac80211 from exposing the management frame cipher suites required
for Protected Management Frames (802.11w).

On networks where PMF is required, association starts but
wpa_supplicant fails while installing the IGTK:

  key setting validation failed
  WPA: Failed to configure IGTK to the driver
  RSN: Failed to configure IGTK

Advertise MFP_CAPABLE so mac80211 can provide the BIP/CMAC/GMAC
management frame ciphers.

Tested on an Orange Pi Zero with XR819 and Linux
6.18.48-current-sunxi. Before this change, iw did not expose
management frame ciphers. Afterwards it exposes CMAC, CMAC-256,
GMAC-128, and GMAC-256, and the device remains connected to an access
point that requires PMF.

Signed-off-by: Mayur Panchal <mayur@canva.com>
---
 main.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/main.c b/main.c
index a30c604..dd64ec1 100644
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -267,6 +267,7 @@ struct ieee80211_hw *xradio_init_common(size_t hw_priv_data_len)
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SUPPORTS_DYNAMIC_PS);
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, REPORTS_TX_ACK_STATUS);
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, CONNECTION_MONITOR);
+	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, MFP_CAPABLE);
 
 /*	hw->flags = IEEE80211_HW_SIGNAL_DBM            |
 	            IEEE80211_HW_SUPPORTS_PS           |
